# Notebook outputs never enter git (task 13).
#
# Committed outputs previously caused an HTTP 400 push failure on this
# repository -- VisualisationResults.ipynb alone carries 2.1 MB of base64
# figure data. The clean filter strips them on the way into the index;
# the working copy keeps its rendered outputs, so nothing is lost locally.
#
# A filter defined here is inert until each clone registers the command
# once (git does not let a repository configure that itself, by design):
#
#     git config filter.nbstrip.clean "python scripts/nbstrip.py --filter"
#     git config filter.nbstrip.smudge cat
#
# Without it notebooks are committed as-is, which is the pre-existing
# behaviour, not a breakage. See the README's "Notebook outputs" note.
*.ipynb filter=nbstrip

# Keep git from trying to diff or merge the generated figures.
*.pdf binary
*.png binary
